    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Make a video explaining how password reset works in our web app: the user says they forgot their password, the app looks up their account, emails them a one-time link, and the user opens it and chooses a new password."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I've drawn the graph: the user, the web app, the accounts database, and the email service. The app looks up the account, sends a reset link by email, and the user opens that link and sets a new password.\n\nDoes the graph look right? Should I add or rename anything before we plan the story?",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The graph looks good. I approve it."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Graph approved. Next is the story. Here's my proposal:\n\n- **Audience:** Customer support staff, or anyone on the team who needs to explain password reset to users. *(Or should this be aimed at end users?)*\n- **Takeaway:** A reset link works once, and only for a short time.\n- **Shape:** Problem, how it works, outcome.\n- **Hook:** \"Someone can't remember their password, so they ask for help.\"\n\nThe video would walk through the four steps: the user asks, the app finds the account, the email with the link goes out, and the user sets a new password. It would end with the user signed in.\n\nDoes this story work? Tell me if you'd change the audience, the takeaway, or the hook.",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Yes, that story works for me. Go ahead and write the script."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I've written the script: one scene with six beats. It runs about 37 seconds, a little under the 45 to 90 seconds I'd aim for. It opens on the user forgetting their password, walks through the app finding the account, the one-time link going out and arriving by email, and the user opening it, and ends with the user signed in.\n\nShould I approve the script as it is, or would you like changes? If you want it longer, I can add a beat on what happens when the link expires.",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The script looks good. I approve it."
      },
